---
import Page from '../components/Page.astro'
---
<Page currentPath="/about" title="About — Jhelum Labs" description="Jhelum Labs is an independent AI research and development organization dedicated to building advanced AI models and contributing to responsible artificial intelligence.">
  <div class="ab-page shell">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="ab-header">
      <h1 class="ab-title">About Jhelum Labs</h1>
      <p class="ab-tagline">Advancing Artificial Intelligence Through Research and Engineering</p>
    </header>

    <div class="ab-body">

      <!-- Intro -->
      <p class="ab-lead">
        Jhelum Labs is an independent artificial intelligence research and development
        initiative dedicated to building advanced AI models, exploring new machine
        learning techniques, and contributing to the development of capable, reliable,
        and responsible artificial intelligence.
      </p>
      <p>
        We believe that advancing AI requires more than simply using existing technologies.
        It requires understanding how models work, experimenting with new architectures,
        developing training systems, evaluating model capabilities, and continuously
        improving the methods used to build intelligent systems.
      </p>

      <!-- Our Work -->
      <h2>Our Work</h2>
      <p>
        Our work focuses on the research, engineering, and development of artificial
        intelligence systems, with an emphasis on language models and modern machine learning.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI Model Development</strong> — Designing, training, and improving language models and other AI systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Machine Learning Research</strong> — Exploring model architectures, training methodologies, optimization techniques, and approaches to improving model performance.</li>
        <li><strong>AI Safety and Reliability</strong> — Investigating model limitations, evaluation methods, robustness, and responsible approaches to AI development.</li>
        <li><strong>Research and Experimentation</strong> — Conducting technical experiments, documenting results, and developing research papers that communicate our methods and findings.</li>
        <li><strong>Open Research</strong> — Sharing research, technical documentation, and model resources where appropriate to support transparency, learning, and collaboration.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- Model Development -->
      <h2>Our Model Development</h2>
      <p>
        Jhelum Labs develops its own experimental AI model series, including the
        <strong>W-1.1 family</strong>. Through these projects, we explore the practical
        challenges of building language models — from data preparation and tokenization
        to model architecture, training, evaluation, and inference.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each experiment provides an opportunity to learn, test ideas, identify limitations,
        and improve our engineering practices. Our longer-term direction is to develop
        increasingly capable AI systems through systematic experimentation and research.
      </p>

      <!-- Three pillars -->
      <div class="ab-cards">
        <div class="ab-card">
          <h3>W-1.1</h3>
          <p>123M-parameter decoder-only Transformer. RoPE, RMSNorm, SwiGLU, 32K BPE vocab, 2,048-token context. Trained on H100 80 GB.</p>
          <a href="/research/w-1.1-final-architecture">Read architecture →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-card">
          <h3>W-1.2 Roadmap</h3>
          <p>353M parameters, grouped-query attention, 50K vocab, 4,096-token context, 8B token training target.</p>
          <a href="/research/w-1.2-architecture">Read roadmap →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-card">
          <h3>Open Weights</h3>
          <p>All released weights are published under Apache-2.0 with SHA-256 verification. Download and run locally with the provided generate.py.</p>
          <a href="/playground">Get started →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Approach -->
      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>
        We approach AI development through a combination of scientific curiosity,
        engineering discipline, iterative experimentation, and technical documentation.
        We value measurable progress over unsupported claims and believe that publishing
        methods, acknowledging limitations, and evaluating systems carefully are important
        parts of responsible AI research.
      </p>
      <p>
        We aim to make our work understandable and useful to developers, researchers,
        students, and others interested in the future of artificial intelligence.
      </p>

      <!-- Mission -->
      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Our mission is to advance artificial intelligence through independent research,
        original model development, and responsible engineering. We aspire to contribute
        useful knowledge, build capable AI systems, and make meaningful progress in
        machine learning through continuous experimentation and open scientific inquiry.
      </p>

      <!-- Looking Ahead -->
      <h2>Looking Ahead</h2>
      <p>
        As we continue developing our model series and research projects, Jhelum Labs
        remains focused on learning, innovation, and long-term progress in artificial
        intelligence. We see every model, experiment, and research paper as part of a
        broader effort to understand and advance the possibilities of AI.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        Jhelum Labs — Building AI. Advancing Research. Exploring What Comes Next.
      </blockquote>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For research inquiries, technical discussions, collaborations, or general
        questions, contact us at:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:team@jhelumlabs.in">team@jhelumlabs.in</a><br/>
        <strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://jhelumlabs.in">https://jhelumlabs.in</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="ab-cta" href="/contact">Contact research team →</a>
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
.ab-page {
  padding: clamp(64px, 9vw, 108px) 0 clamp(80px, 11vw, 130px);
}

/* Header */
.ab-header {
  max-width: 780px;
  margin-bottom: 56px;
  padding-bottom: 40px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
}
.ab-title {
  font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.8rem);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  line-height: 1.05;
  color: var(--text);
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.ab-tagline {
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
  color: var(--text-soft);
  margin: 0;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* Body */
.ab-body {
  max-width: 720px;
}
.ab-lead {
  font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
  line-height: 1.72;
  color: var(--text-soft);
  margin: 0 0 1.2em;
}
.ab-body p {
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.78;
  color: var(--text-soft);
  margin: 0 0 1.1em;
}
.ab-body h2 {
  font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: var(--text);
  margin: 2.4em 0 0.7em;
  padding-top: 1.2em;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line-subtle);
}
.ab-body h2:first-of-type {
  border-top: none;
  padding-top: 0;
}
.ab-body ul {
  padding-left: 1.2em;
  margin: 0 0 1.2em;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 10px;
}
.ab-body li {
  font-size: .97rem;
  line-height: 1.65;
  color: var(--text-soft);
}
.ab-body strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600 }
.ab-body a {
  color: var(--text);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
  transition: opacity .15s;
}
.ab-body a:hover { opacity: .7 }
.ab-body blockquote {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  padding: 4px 0 4px 20px;
  margin: 2em 0;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--text-soft);
  line-height: 1.6;
}

/* Cards */
.ab-cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
  margin: 1.5em 0 2em;
}
.ab-card {
  padding: 22px 24px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: var(--surface-card);
}
.ab-card h3 {
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  letter-spacing: -.015em;
}
.ab-card p {
  font-size: .84rem;
  color: var(--text-soft);
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin: 0 0 12px;
}
.ab-card a {
  font-size: .82rem;
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* CTA button */
.ab-cta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  padding: 11px 24px;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--text);
  color: var(--bg) !important;
  font-size: .9rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  transition: opacity .15s ease;
}
.ab-cta:hover { opacity: .85 }

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .ab-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr }
}
</style>
